[2026-01-14T01:20:25.999107] I have created the test runner. It performs a differential test, comparing the output of the sequential and parallel implementations for various test cases (empty, small, medium, large). It also includes a determinism check by running the parallel version twice and comparing the hashes of the results. A performance check mode is included for large inputs.

I've structured the test runner to be self-contained and aliased the structs to keep the sequential and parallel code separate for testing, even though they share the same underlying struct definition. The runner will exit with a non-zero status code on failure, which is good for automation.

